                <pb facs="0647" n="545" sameAs="frus:frus1919v01/pg545"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">893.51/2573: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Chargé in China</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Tenney</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Peking</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1919-12-09T16:00:00+08:00"><hi rendition="#italic">December 9,
                                1919, 4 p.m.</hi></date><lb/>[<hi rendition="#italic">Received
                            December 9, 3 p.m.</hi>]</dateline></opener>
                <p>Referring to Department’s telegram of December 8 [<hi rendition="#italic"
                    >4</hi>], 4 p.m. I informed bankers on their arrival the Legation could not
                    support loan without instructions from the Department. Bankers decided to go
                    ahead without waiting for approval of the Department. The Chinese Minister of
                    Finance informs me that the five million has already been paid by Pacific
                    Development Corporation. Reorganization of Wine and Tobacco Administration is
                    understood to be proceeding according to the terms of the loan agreement.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Tenney</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
